WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Let’s deploy AOS Work on a single Linux server.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.567
Point your domains at the server. Open ports 80 and 443.

00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:12.300
Using local MinIO? You’ll need a storage domain, too.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.967
Download deploy.sh from the release linked in the guide.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.900
In Termius, upload the script to this folder using SFTP.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:25.533
Open the server terminal and type the command you see here.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.900
Press Enter to start the checks.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.433
The installer checks your processor, memory, and deployment disk.

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:36.500
Look at total capacity. You need a hundred gigabytes.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:40.700
Both ports say free. Nginx can use them on this host.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:44.900
Each domain gets its own HTTP and HTTPS check.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.400
This server still needs Docker, Nginx, and Certbot.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.700
Type y, then press Enter to install the missing tools.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:00.500
See “Environment ready”? Now you can configure your domains.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.100
In the main menu, choose one for domains and HTTPS.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.660
Choose one again for AOS Work.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.020
Type the host name that points to your server,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.500
then press Enter.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.580
Choose two for Studio.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.260
With local MinIO, choose three for Storage as well.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:21.220
Wait for the saved HTTPS address after each domain,

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.740
then choose zero to return.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.540
Choose two to select a server package.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.980
The latest package is listed first.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.100
Choose one.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.660
The package includes the repository's preset resources.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:38.100
Wait for “Server package ready”.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.300
Now choose three to deploy applications.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.180
Take a moment to read the list.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:47.533
Choose three again to install Studio and AOS Work together.

00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:52.633
For PostgreSQL, choose one to run it on this server.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.400
Press Enter for the default username, then set a password.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:03.400
The password stays hidden as you type. Press Enter, then type it again to confirm.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.200
Postgres and its vector extension are ready.

00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:11.233
For Redis, choose one to use the local Docker Compose service.

00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:15.433
Give Redis its own password.

00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:20.633
For RabbitMQ, choose one to run it locally.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:24.733
Accept the default username and set a RabbitMQ password.

00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:29.866
For object storage, choose one to deploy MinIO locally.

00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:32.600
Set and confirm its password.

00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:35.866
Using hosted middleware? Choose External service.

00:02:35.867 --> 00:02:37.427
Once the middleware is ready,

00:02:37.427 --> 00:02:41.147
set the default password for new AOS Work users.

00:02:41.147 --> 00:02:43.987
Type it, press Enter, and type it again.

00:02:43.987 --> 00:02:46.187
The terminal keeps your input hidden.

00:02:46.187 --> 00:02:50.507
Studio then asks for a separate password to protect encrypted data.

00:02:50.507 --> 00:02:52.227
Enter and confirm it.

00:02:52.227 --> 00:02:58.987
This release uses Studio backend 1.8.12 and frontend 1.8.14.

00:02:58.987 --> 00:03:03.027
On a single server, enter zero for the sandbox host ID.

00:03:03.027 --> 00:03:04.867
Press Enter to continue.

00:03:04.867 --> 00:03:07.467
After the AOS Work health check passes,

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:10.107
look for the administrator sign-in details.

00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:15.187
On a fresh installation, sign in as admin with the default password shown here.

00:03:15.187 --> 00:03:17.147
Change it when you first sign in.

00:03:17.147 --> 00:03:20.307
Existing installations keep their current credentials.

00:03:20.307 --> 00:03:23.187
To update a service later, choose four.

00:03:23.187 --> 00:03:26.347
For example, choose two for the Studio frontend,

00:03:26.347 --> 00:03:28.627
then enter the image tag you want.

00:03:28.627 --> 00:03:31.347
Choose five to see the restart options.

00:03:31.347 --> 00:03:33.667
Zero returns to the main menu.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.907
Choose six for the health report.

00:03:35.907 --> 00:03:38.947
Look for running services and passing health checks.

00:03:38.947 --> 00:03:42.747
The storage initialization job runs once and then exits.

00:03:42.747 --> 00:03:45.027
When the summary says all healthy,

00:03:45.027 --> 00:03:48.267
open the secure addresses and check the sign-in pages.
